<!-- Section 6: Strategic Recommendations -->
<div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-number">6</div>
        <h2>Key Findings & Strategic Recommendations</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Key Findings</h3>
        <ul class="rec-list">
            <li>
                <strong>Condition is the dominant profit driver.</strong>
                Deadstock items average {fmt_usd(ds_data['avg_profit'])} profit with a {fmt_pct(ds_data['pct_profitable'])} profitability rate, while Used items average {fmt_usd(used_data['avg_profit'])} with only {fmt_pct(used_data['pct_profitable'])} profitable. VNDS sits between at {fmt_usd(vnds_data['avg_profit'])} avg profit and {fmt_pct(vnds_data['pct_profitable'])} profitability.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Premium colorways outperform regardless of model.</strong>
                {kpis['top_colorway']} leads all colorways with an average margin of {fmt_usd(kpis['top_colorway_margin'])}. The top-performing model-colorway combinations are concentrated among hype-driven and limited-release colorways.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Channel selection creates meaningful margin differentiation.</strong>
                The spread between the highest and lowest-margin channels is {fmt_usd(channel_stats[0]['avg_profit'] - channel_stats[-1]['avg_profit'])}, meaning channel selection alone can swing a transaction from profitable to loss-making.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Inventory velocity varies significantly across platforms.</strong>
                The fastest channels average ~{min(c['avg_days'] for c in channel_stats):.0f} days while the slowest reach ~{max(c['avg_days'] for c in channel_stats):.0f} days. This 2-3x spread in holding time affects capital efficiency and risk exposure.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>The market shows overall positive economics.</strong>
                With a {kpis['resale_premium_rate']}% premium rate and {kpis['avg_resale_to_retail']:.2f}x average resale-to-retail ratio, the Air Jordan resale market remains profitable at scale, though individual transaction outcomes vary widely (std. dev: {fmt_usd(pd_dist['std'])}).
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Strategic Recommendations</h3>
        <ul class="rec-list">
            <li>
                <strong>Prioritize Deadstock sourcing above all else.</strong>
                The {fmt_usd(ds_premium_over_used)} resale premium and {ds_data['pct_profitable'] - used_data['pct_profitable']:.0f}pp profitability advantage over Used pairs makes Deadstock the only condition tier worth sourcing at scale. VNDS is acceptable for high-demand colorways only.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Focus sourcing on high-margin model-colorway combinations.</strong>
                Concentrate capital on the top-15 combinations identified in Section 2. Avoid bottom-10 combinations entirely — these consistently underperform regardless of channel or holding period.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Match channel to product and urgency.</strong>
                For high-value Deadstock pairs where margin is the priority, use higher-margin channels even at the cost of longer hold times. For VNDS or time-sensitive inventory, prioritize faster-turnover platforms to reduce capital lock-up and depreciation risk.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Implement seasonal timing strategies.</strong>
                Use the monthly seasonality patterns in Section 5 to time purchases (during lower-margin months) and sales (during peak-margin periods). Even small timing advantages compound across a portfolio.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Monitor the margin-velocity quadrant.</strong>
                Continuously track the scatter relationship between channel margin and days-in-inventory. Optimal portfolio allocation shifts inventory toward the upper-left quadrant (high margin, fast turnover) and away from the lower-right (low margin, slow turnover).
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

